       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). The 1600 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nHere are some typical regimens:\n- **Mild to moderate pain or inflammation:** 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours as needed, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Anti-inflammatory use, such as arthritis:** 600\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n\nWas the intended dose 400 mg or 800 mg, or was the total meant to be 1600 mg per day? If you tell me the dose and frequency you want, I'll enter it. If you do want the original dose, please confirm that it's intentional and give me a clinical rationale for the order note."
